.TH OS-BUILDER-CLI 1 "November 2026" "os-builder 3.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
os-builder-cli \- remaster Ubuntu images from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B os-builder-cli
.RB [ \-w
.IR workspace ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B preflight
Check the host for the required tools.
.TP
.BI inspect " iso"
List the squashfs file systems of an ISO.
.TP
.BI extract " iso"
Extract an ISO into the workspace
.RB ( \-\-layer ,
.BR \-\-replace ).
.TP
.B shell
Root shell inside the image.
.TP
.BI customize " file.json"
Apply a customization file.
.TP
.BI build " output.iso"
Repack and build the ISO
.RB ( \-\-volume\-id ,
.BR \-\-compression ,
.BR \-\-config ,
.BR "\-\-boot\-mode hybrid" | uefi ).
.TP
.B boot\-info
Show how the extracted image boots: legacy BIOS, UEFI, Secure Boot.
.TP
.B synaptic
Run Synaptic inside the image on the current X display.
.TP
.B desktop
Run the image's desktop session in a Xephyr window
.RB ( \-\-resolution ).
.TP
.B cleanup
Unmount leftovers of a crashed session.
.TP
.B delete
Delete the extracted image.
.PP
All commands except
.B preflight
and
.B inspect
need root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR os-builder (1)
